title: "Odin OS: Cryptographically Authorized Memory Mutation in a RISC-V PMP-Enforced Agent Execution Environment"
authors:
  - family-names: Walker
    given-names: Nathan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-0965-4424"
    affiliation: "Ravenhelm Platform & Runestack Research"
version: "0.1.0-rc.b32"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23928301"
date-released: "2026-11-07"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nwalker85/odinos"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23928301"
abstract: >-
  Odin OS is a bare-metal, zero-allocation (#![no_std]) 64-bit RISC-V microkernel
  investigating cryptographically authorized memory mutation for autonomous AI agents.
  By coupling cache-line aligned Ed25519-signed TransitionDeeds with hardware Physical
  Memory Protection (PMP) comparators, Odin OS enforces physical wordline gating (WE=0)
  against unauthorized agent mutations at memory-bus speeds.
keywords:
  - risc-v
  - microkernel
  - physical-memory-protection
  - pmp
  - capability-based-security
  - ai-safety
  - autonomous-agents
  - formal-verification
  - smt
